infographic compare-hierarchy-row-letter-card-rounded-rect-node
data
  title Three file primitives, three jobs
  compares
    - label O_EXCL — create-if-absent
      children
        - label Use: single-instance lock or claim a work item
        - label Wins: atomic for one caller; the rest get EEXIST
        - label Risk: a crashed owner leaves a stale lock file
    - label temp + fsync + rename — atomic replace
      children
        - label Use: crash-safe overwrite of a file readers see
        - label Wins: every reader and crash sees whole old or whole new
        - label Risk: same filesystem only — across devices fails with EXDEV
    - label flock — advisory lock
      children
        - label Use: coordinate cooperating processes
        - label Wins: self-cleaning — the lock dies with its descriptor
        - label Risk: advisory, same-machine, weak over NFS
theme
  palette #6366f1 #14b8a6 #f59e0b
